     Note     🙋 Why use  .get()  here instead of a  useStore  helper?   You may have noticed we’re calling  cartItems.get()  here, instead of grabbing that  useStore  helper from our React / Preact / Solid / Vue examples. This is because  useStore is meant to trigger component re-renders.  In other words,  useStore  should be used whenever the store value is being rendered to the UI. Since we’re reading the value when an  event  is triggered ( addToCart  in this case), and we aren’t trying to render that value, we don’t need  useStore  here.    
